# Fabric Awning and Scallop Seam

Status: DONE
Milestone: M21 Bounded interactive fabric
Dependencies: 23_FULL_WIDTH_AWNING_AND_PLAIN_HERO.todo; 25_WOODEN_BACKLIT_SHOP_SIGN.todo

## Purpose

The owner wants the full-width page awning to react like cloth to a cursor on or
near it and to scrolling. They also questioned lines at the patterned green
section's scalloped edge. Keep the existing art, palette, rails, width and copy.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve original runtime, styling, tests, public overview and context.
- [x] Implement a bounded damped spring mesh with fixed rails and local response.
- [x] Render the original awning texture at bounded high resolution, without seams.
- [x] Connect nearby fine-pointer input and signed scroll impulses.
- [x] Stop after settling; retain exact static fallback and preference gates.
- [x] Measure the story-edge shadow mismatch; remove the extra inset shadow.
- [x] Exercise cursor/near/scroll, pinned rail, settling, idle and lifecycle behavior.
- [x] Run existing full site/asset checks; keep baseline entry-focus issue separate.
- [x] Refresh the story README image and public descriptions.
- [x] Publish only allowlisted modules/styles and affected public docs/showcase.

## Acceptance criteria

- Local cloth deformation, not rigid whole-awning tilt or movement of navigation.
- Top rail/front bar/side anchors fixed; exact original SVG returns after release.
- Pointer influence within72px; touch does not intercept scrolling.
- Scroll response works in both directions; reduced-motion/forced-colour/print stay static.
- No continuous idle frame loop, unbounded field growth or external dependencies.
- GPU loss/missing modules/unsupported WebGL retain original artwork and links.
- Canvas is decorative, aria-hidden, click-through and confined to the page awning.
- Background cream/green pattern stays static; no rejected cream renderer restored.
- Green scallops retained without the extra darker inset-shadow strip.
- No new image-tool views or owner acceptance claimed.

